# Keep the click-to-run Windows script as CRLF.
#
# cmd.exe is mostly forgiving about line endings, but not entirely — a label or
# a `goto` in a file with bare LF endings can be misread, and this is a file
# whose whole job is to work when a person double-clicks it on a machine nobody
# here can test. Git is told plainly rather than left to guess from a core
# setting that differs per checkout.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# And the shell scripts as LF, for the same reason in the other direction: a
# CRLF shebang line makes the interpreter "not found".
*.sh text eol=lf
